hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1394","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of a man called Hanash, on the authority of Ali, h. Muhammad bin Yahya and Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr narrated to us, Al-Hakam narrated to me, On the authority of a man called Hanash, on the authority of Ali, Muhammad bin Yahya said, and this is the hadith of Ahmad, he said: “The sun was eclipsed and Ali led the people in prayer, so he mentioned Hadith, and they said: He stood up in the second rak’ah, and did the same as he did in the first rak’ah, then he sat praying and praying until the sun rose, then he spoke to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that. Yusuf said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did that."
